Description: live dashboard of every progress bar on the desktop
 MetaMonitor is a GTK 4 / libadwaita window that gathers progress from
 many sources into one GPU-drawn dashboard:
  - Claude Code sessions, their background commands and jobs;
  - any command run through mmrun, piped into mmctl pipe or followed with
    mmctl tail (percentages, OSC 9;4, GRASS, GDAL and N/M counters);
  - scripts writing a percentage into a slot file with mmctl set;
  - cp, dd, tar, rsync, gzip, sha256sum and similar commands, read from
    /proc with no setup;
  - applications broadcasting Unity LauncherEntry progress over D-Bus;
  - GRASS GIS sessions found from mapset .gislock files, with exact module
    progress from a small G_percent() shim preloaded through the GRASS env
    file, and stale locks flagged.
